; KNOWN-FAILING (VM-compile panic): `load-wav` bound to a LOCAL rather
; than assigned to a dynamic global. The VM's cpu-mode lowering only
; matches the whole-global-assignment pattern (`HostOp::AssignDynFromWav`
; writes into a global's dyn region), so a value-position call falls
; through to the generic builtin compiler's todo!(). The tree-walker
; handles it fine.
@cpu
(defn main []
  (let [samples (load-wav "data/audio/test_sample.wav")]
    (print (array-length samples))))
